  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_194e355596b24909ab770086f4be493b",
      "statement": "FrozenArmMixin._register_frozen_arm applies the uniform frozen-arm prep once at construction: it calls arm.eval(), sets requires_grad_(False) on every parameter, registers the arm as a normal nn.Module submodule via setattr (so Lightning's automatic .to(device) owns its placement), and adds the name to the _frozen_arm_names frozenset, whose class-level default is an empty frozenset so a host with no frozen arms degrades to a no-op instead of AttributeError.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L50-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d06bef4d34e642212da808617846e6929e11ee815fa2d97ef914ac9e94817e60:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_41821829d0944fb39e1b0c68e1495960",
      "statement": "The mixin's state_dict override keeps frozen arms off the checkpoint by deleting their keys in place from the shared destination dict and matching them under the caller-supplied prefix, so a frozen arm cannot leak into a checkpoint collected through a wrapper or DDP's 'module.' prefix (PyTorch discards the child's return value and reads the destination it passed in).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L82-L105",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19414104e9bdf43116dce701b0afa36a6380b2553b09a125335ff357101a56ab:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71355d3231ab4284992dbfc41bc995fd",
      "statement": "The mixin's load_state_dict override is strict on the trainable keys and lenient only on the registered frozen arms: it strips stray frozen keys from the incoming dict, loads with strict=False, then raises a RuntimeError naming 'missing'/'unexpected' for any non-frozen mismatch when strict=True — the frozen arms' absence from the checkpoint is the single tolerated mismatch, and there is no blanket strict=False that would hide a missing trainable key.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L107-L138",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f0cb03d88c3fca2831aad4e930fe3a8d9cb078a961eedaab02122cea0c2993b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d4bc63a8fe9945ef9657945bada29f18",
      "statement": "The mixin's train(mode) override re-applies eval() to every registered frozen arm after super().train(mode), because registration makes Lightning's recursive train(True) flip the arms back to training mode, which would let a frozen arm's BatchNorm running stats drift during rollout or reward evaluation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/frozen_arm.py#L140-L154",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f4ad8ae48c456480b02b363184c35777d7e60e21d3463710ef0369b94866962:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d9aa1ec4130648f68bfcb16c7d390dd2",
      "statement": "The mixin deliberately does not own optimizer arm selection: each host keeps its own configure_optimizers, which builds Adam over the trainable arm only (GRPOModule: controlnet on the ControlNet policy or unet on the UNet policy; RewardModule: reward_model; ControlNetLatentFlowModule: controlnet), while the mixin contributes only the requires_grad=False layer and the checkpoint overrides.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/modules/controlnet_latent_flow.py#L271-L280",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f3047c27d35707c30d8e1ef4d1ca6bdb86d1b2f93280ed38124778bf052fa19:"
