    {
      "id": "claim_91c69cdcb5cd4724b30987e532765ad3",
      "statement": "The JiT shell does not pin: it keeps a bare launch-time torch.device('cuda' if torch.cuda.is_available() else 'cpu'), builds the VAE on CPU before the process group exists so nothing is staged on a GPU, and resolves the per-rank device only in the post-process-group warm closure via DevicePolicy().warm_device(device); the controlnet _real_inputs warm closure resolves it the same way.",
