    {
      "id": "claim_8baf51ac9b924b329f55be82acb0c00a",
      "statement": "Registering the frozen arms gives up one invariant the old object.__setattr__ bypass had: at DistributedDataParallel construction every registered parameter, including the requires_grad=False frozen arms, is broadcast from rank 0 — a one-time startup cost GRPO pays several times (base + reward + reference UNet + reference ControlNet) that can compound DDP-init timeout pressure; the documented mitigation is to construct the arms identically on every rank rather than adding a DDP exclusion hack, and DDP keeps the default broadcast_buffers=True with find_unused_parameters=True unchanged.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0031-device-ownership.md#L152-L165",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ab4775d9622ac2ee0a21cf40bb8dee35a0a1e1a72bd33760b1f0337e5b6582c2:"
        },
        {
